    kind: 'enzyme',
    summary: 'The low-capacity, high-affinity conjugation pathway. Because its cofactor pool is small and easily depleted, a large phenolic load from food or a botanical can saturate sulfation and change the metabolic fate of an unrelated substrate — and for the allylbenzenes, sulfonation is the step that makes a metabolite reactive rather than safe.',
